{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"regional-lamproite-flee","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n\nWhen a ticket records no `file_impact`, attestation currency falls back to invalidating on ANY code-SHA change — a deliberate fail-safe, but measured to over-trigger badly: 307 of 1,457 full-LLM plan re-reviews (21%) ran on byte-identical material fingerprints, 171 of them triggered by base-SHA drift alone (analysis ticket b902-18af-14ed-4da1). Allowing drift without re-review and requiring file_impact universally are both rejected; the approved design scopes the fail-safe instead.\n\n## Plan (approved components a + b)\n\n(a) **Record the review's read-set.** The agentic passes already observe which repository files they open (`distinct_fetches` in the usage telemetry). Persist that read-set (paths only) into the plan-review sidecar payload alongside `verified_at_sha`, as the review's measured dependency basis.\n\n(b) **Diff-intersect on drift.** When the attestation's SHA no longer matches and no `file_impact` is recorded, compute `git diff --name-only <attested_sha>..<current>` and invalidate ONLY when a changed path intersects (read-set ∪ plan-cited paths ∪ a small fixed blast-radius list: criteria registry, reviewer prompts, gate config). Empty intersection → attestation stays current. Any failure to compute the diff or read the recorded set falls back to today's invalidate-on-any-change, so the fail-safe is never weaker than the status quo.\n\nA review that read no code and cites no code (a genuinely no-code ticket) has an empty basis and stops re-triggering on unrelated code motion — the original complaint — while a review that DID consult code is invalidated exactly when consulted or cited material moves.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The plan-review sidecar payload records the agentic passes' distinct repository read paths for reviews where any agentic pass ran (absent/empty otherwise). Verify: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit -k \"sidecar and read\" -x` passes with a new test pinning the field.\n- [ ] With no file_impact recorded and a moved SHA, currency evaluation invalidates iff `git diff --name-only` between the attested and current SHA intersects read-set ∪ cited paths ∪ the blast-radius list; a disjoint diff leaves the attestation current. Verify: unit tests cover both directions.\n- [ ] Diff-computation failure, missing read-set on a pre-change attestation, and unreadable recorded paths each fall back to invalidate (fail-safe preserved). Verify: unit tests cover each fallback.\n- [ ] `rebar review-plan <id> --status` reports which basis (file_impact | read-set | fail-safe) currency was decided on. Verify: CLI output assertion in tests.","id":"81ca-9443-3443-4d27","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Scope no-file-impact SHA-drift invalidation to the review read-set and cited paths (approved design a+b)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786486337715312001,"uuid":"1dda8f05-dbb2-4bd5-8474-834610d32f05"}